{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_TQn6lFSHEBG8YQAwgMn1zQwQ","content":"130\trestate a rule** (for example \"an order has exactly one amount\"), and the guideline repeats\n131\tdescriptions as written, escaped onto one line. Read it as guidance about meaning, never as a rule\n132\tto enforce while extracting. No description, reading or name can start a heading. The file is\n133\tplain text in Markdown layout: raw HTML in a description is not escaped, so read the file as\n134\ttext and do not render it.\n135\t\n136\t## 5. Failure semantics\n137\t\n138\t| What happened | Machine-readable form | Exit | What you do |\n139\t|---|---|---|---|\n140\t| The population file does not parse | population fails to load | 3 | re-emit the whole file (§2); never hand-repair |\n141\t| The sidecar is absent | `extraction:sidecar-missing`, state `failed` | 3 | write it; absence is a FAILURE, never a skip |\n142\t| The sidecar has an unknown field, a missing digest, or an unsafe path | `extraction:sidecar-invalid`, state `failed` | 3 | fix the sidecar against §3 |\n143\t| A recorded digest does not match the file bytes | `extraction:binding-mismatch`, state `failed` | 3 | recompute digests after the last write and rewrite the sidecar |\n144\t| The header disagrees with the model | `extraction:header-mismatch`, state `failed` | 3 | re-copy `header_template` verbatim (§4) |\n145\t| The checker found an alethic violation | verdicts on the checker channel, state `ran` | 1 | REPORT IT — the document describes a world that violates the model |\n146\t| The population is vacuous | state `ran` | 2 | report it; a document that supports no facts is a finding |\n147\t| The checker could not decide | state `ran` | 4 | report it |\n148\t| Everything held | state `ran` | 0 | report it |\n149\t\n150\tThe three states are `ran`, `skipped` and `failed`. **`skipped` is written only by the intentional opt-out `gnd verify --no-extraction`** — you never write it, and a missing file never produces it. A measurement that did not happen must not read as green.\n151\t\n152\tExit 0 with state `ran` is **checker acceptance**, not proof of faithfulness. A hallucinated, well-shaped, conforming population exits 0. That is a real extractor error and it is exactly what `gnd fidelity` exists to measure; nothing in a `verify` payload speaks to it, and no rate ever appears there.\n153\t\n154\t## 6. What is out of scope\n155\t\n156\t- **Verifier-guided repair** — re-reading the verdict and adjusting facts until the population passes. Deferred by name to EXP-02. It makes the extraction a function of the checker and destroys the independence the measurement rests on.\n157\t- **Choosing the header.** §4.\n158\t- **Calibration.** The round trip measures the round trip; recall is flattered because a renderer authored the ground truth. `gnd fidelity` reports `calibration.state: \"uncalibrated\"` and `publishable: false`, and emits no interval at all while that holds. Do not present a fidelity number as a quality claim.\n159\t"}
